      "width": 1000,
      "height": 671,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "Public domain",
      "artist": "Unknown author",
      "description": "Observatory, Wickham Terrace, Brisbane, Queensland, ca. 1908.\nThe old windmill observatory on Wickham Terrace, Brisbane, around 1908. Four flags are flying on the mast in front of the mill. A lamp post and telegraph pole can be seen on the opposite corner. Copied from a postcard, the back of which reads: 'Dear Sister, Just a P.C. to let you know I am still in the land of the living and in stale old Brisbane. I am not settled but will write when I am as I am not sure when I will be going away. Tomorrow is your birthday and I sincerely wish you very many happy returns of the day and trust you are enjoying the best of health. I must conclude with -?. Best love to you all. You will get my address from Alex. I had a letter from Eva last week. Hope you will like the card. I remain your loving sister, Lilly.'.",
      "dateCreated": "circa 1908<div style=\"display: none;\">date QS:P,+1908-00-00T00:00:00Z/9,P1480,Q5727902</div>",
      "sourceType": "commons-category",
      "sourceArticleId": "the-old-windmill-brisbane-wp",
      "sourceGeohash4": "r7hg"
    },
